Smart Crane Control System using Industrial Shields ESP32 PLC14

This project is a smart crane control system developed using the Industrial Shields ESP32 PLC14 and a BLE-based mobile application. The system enables wireless crane operation, real-time monitoring, and web-based configuration management.

Features
BLE Mobile App Control

The ESP32 PLC14 connects with a BLE mobile application to control crane operations wirelessly. The mobile app provides control for the following crane motions and safety functions:

UP motion control
DOWN motion control
Emergency Stop (E-STOP)

The BLE connection allows operators to control the crane safely and conveniently from a mobile device.

Integrated Webserver

The PLC14 hosts a built-in webserver for monitoring and configuration purposes.

Webserver Functions
Real-Time Monitoring

The web dashboard displays:

BLE mobile app connection status
Current crane motion status
UP
DOWN
STOP
E-STOP status

This allows operators and administrators to monitor the system in real time from any browser connected to the same network.

User Management System

The webserver includes a user management section for BLE app authentication.

Features
Add new users
Manage BLE app login credentials
Restrict unauthorized access to crane controls
This improves system security and access control.

Output Configuration Page

The system also provides an output configuration page through the webserver.
Features
Configure PLC output pin assignments
Dynamically change output mappings without modifying firmware
Flexible setup for different crane wiring configurations

Technologies Used
Industrial Shields ESP32 PLC14
ESP32 BLE
Embedded Webserver
HTML / CSS / JavaScript
Arduino Framework
WiFi Communication

Applications
Industrial crane automation
Wireless crane control systems
Smart hoist systems
Industrial IoT monitoring
Remote machine operation
